# C72 deploy: restart app + home screen icon after install

Whenever you install/deploy a new `mokoapp` build to the Chainway C72 (or any connected device):

1. Install with Gradle (`./gradlew :app:installDebug`) or `adb install`, targeting the C72 serial when multiple devices are connected.
2. **Force-stop** the running app, then **start** it again so the new process loads the new build.
3. Starting `MainActivity` also runs `HomeScreenHelper.ensureLauncherShortcut()` (legacy INSTALL_SHORTCUT + pin request). If the launcher shows an “Add to Home screen” prompt, that is expected — accept it once.

```bash
ADB="$HOME/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools/adb"
# Prefer C72 if present
SERIAL=$($ADB devices -l | awk '/model:C72/{print $1; exit}')
SERIAL=${SERIAL:-$($ADB devices | awk '/\tdevice$/{print $1; exit}')}
$ADB -s "$SERIAL" install -r mokoapp/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
$ADB -s "$SERIAL" shell am force-stop com.mokobara.mokoapp
$ADB -s "$SERIAL" shell am start -n com.mokobara.mokoapp/.MainActivity
```

Do this every time after a successful deploy — do not leave the old process running.
